    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Overview of drug treatment for IBD:"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Drugs that reduce gut motility are contraindicated in acute IBD:"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 72,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "o",
      "font": "Courier New",
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Antidiarrheals (loperamide, diphenoxylate/atropine, codeine) – "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "underline",
        "attrs": {
         "style": "single"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "reduce gut motility"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "; risk of "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "underline",
        "attrs": {
         "style": "single"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "precipitating toxic megacolon"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 72,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "o",
      "font": "Courier New",
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Anticholinergics (hyoscyamine, dicyclomine) for intestinal spasm and pain also "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "underline",
        "attrs": {
         "style": "single"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "reduce gut motility"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " and should be avoided in active IBD"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 72,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "o",
      "font": "Courier New",
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Opioid analgesics may significantly "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "underline",
        "attrs": {
         "style": "single"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "reduce GI motility"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "IBS – general approach to treatment "
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Treatment is based on the predominant symptoms (IBS-C, IBS-D, IBS-A) and their severity"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Milder, less frequent episodes can be managed with lifestyle changes such as dietary restrictions, a higher-fiber diet, physical activity, and relaxation techniques"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "More persistent disease may require as-needed uses of various antispasmodic or antidiarrheal agents such as loperamide. "
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The most severe forms of this disease may call for pharmacologic agents directed specifically at the underlying neurohormonal imbalance, such as the 5-HT4 agonists or 5-HT3 -receptor antagonists"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
